  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1202 PM CDT Wed Jul 29 2026\n\nThe relentless summer heat will continue through the end of July \nwith triple-digit high temperatures as ridging aloft prevails. \nHeat index values are expected to be higher than earlier this week\nas well as humidity increases via persistent low level southerly \nto southeasterly flow. Heat headlines may be needed as heat index \nvalues approach 108-110 degrees Saturday afternoon, mainly along \nand east of the I-35 corridor.\n\nThere will be a limited opportunity for isolated to scattered\nshowers and storms across portions of South Central Texas. The\naforementioned ridge aloft is expected to shift west over the\nDesert Southwest, placing our region beneath northwesterly flow.\nThis will allow for a weak frontal boundary to track across South\nCentral Texas late this weekend. However, there are still\ndiscrepancies on the timing of this weak boundary among\ndeterministic guidance on any convective development over the\nweekend, and most precipitation chances are capped at 20% or less\nfor late Saturday afternoon and Sunday. More seasonable\ntemperatures return Sunday and into early next week.",
